ames>RJ</given-names></name></person-group><source>Psychological care of the patient with cancer</source><year>1990</year><publisher-name>Oxford , University Press</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lazarus</surname><given-names>RS</given-names></name></person-group><source>Psychological stress and coping process</source><year>1996</year><publisher-name>Toronto , McGraw Hill</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Carlsson</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Killander</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Omne-Ponten</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Larsson</surname><given-names>UB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Voluntary associations for cancer patients in Sweden: supportive activities</article-title><source>Support Care Cancer</source><year>2001</year><volume>9</volume><fpage>581</fpage><lpage>590</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11762968</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s005200100250</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wijkstr&#x000f6;m</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Ibsen SH</surname></name></person-group><article-title>Social capital and the civil society in Nordic countries</article-title><source>Voluntaries challenges - Nordic research about voluntary work and voluntary organisations</source><year>2001</year><publisher-name>Odense , Odense Universitetsf&#x000f6;rlag</publisher-name><fpage>125</fpage><lpage>145</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wijkstr&#x000f6;m</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Lundstr&#x000f6;m</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><source>The voluntary sector. The organisation in the civil society (Swedish)</source><year>2002</year><publisher-name>Stockholm , Sober F&#x000f6;rlag</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Caron-Flinterman</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name><name><surname>Broerse</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name><name><surname>Bunders</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The experiential knowledge of patients: a new resource for biomedical research?</article-title><source>Soc Sci Med</source><year>2005</year><volume>60</volume><fpage>2575</fpage><lpage>2584</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15814182</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.socscimed.2004.11.023</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Boote</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Telford</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Cooper</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Consumer involvement in health research: a review and research agenda</article-title><source>Health Policy</source><year>2002</year><volume>61</volume><fpage>213</fpage><lpage>236</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12088893</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0168-8510(01)00214-7</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Langton</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Barnes</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Haslehurst</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Rimmer</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Turton</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Collaboration, user involvement and education: a systematic review of the literature and report of an educational initiative</article-title><source>Eur J Oncol Nurs</source><year>2003</year><volume>7</volume><fpage>242</fpage><lpage>252</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14637127</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S1462-3889(03)00033-4</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Oliver</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Milne</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Bradburn</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Buchanan</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Kerridge</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Walley</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Gabbay</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Involving consumers in a needs-led research programme: a pilot project</article-title><source>Health Expect</source><year>2001</year><volume>4</volume><fpage>18</fpage><lpage>28</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11286596</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1046/j.1369-6513.2001.00113.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Weinfurt</surname><given-names>KP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Outcomes research related to patient decision making in oncology</article-title><source>Clin Ther</source><year>2003</year><volume>25</volume><fpage>671</fpage><lpage>683</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12749521</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0149-2918(03)80104-2</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Carlsson</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Nilbert</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Nilsson</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Patients' involvement in improving cancer care: experiences in three years of collaboration between members of patient associations and health care professionals</article-title><source>Patient Educ Couns</source><year>2006</year><volume>61</volume><fpage>65</fpage><lpage>71</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16533678</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.pec.2005.02.008</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mishler</surname><given-names>EG</given-names></name></person-group><source>Reseach interviewing. Context and narrative</source><year>1986</year><publisher-name>Cambridge , MA: Harvard University Press</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>HSFR</collab></person-group><article-title>Ethical Principle for Research in Humanistic and Social Science Research</article-title><year>1990</year></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Edwards</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><source>Discourse and cognition</source><year>1997</year><publisher-name>New Dehli , Thousands Oaks, Sage Publications</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Silverman</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><source>Interpreting qualitative data. Methods for analysing talks, text and interaction</source><year>2001</year><edition>2nd</edition><publisher-name>London , Sage Publications</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="book"><source>Patients&#x02019; right for information and participation</source><year>2001</year><publisher-name>The National Swedish Board of Health and Welfare</publish